WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.474
CMMC is not solely a compliance-team initiative.

00:00:03.474 --> 00:00:08.777
The people who design systems, administer accounts, develop applications, manage contracts,

00:00:08.777 --> 00:00:14.562
operate services, handle information, and oversee suppliers all affect the security outcome.

00:00:14.562 --> 00:00:16.972
Leadership establishes accountability and resources.

00:00:16.972 --> 00:00:21.311
Executives and program owners decide priorities, approve risk decisions,

00:00:21.311 --> 00:00:22.757
resolve ownership conflicts,

00:00:22.757 --> 00:00:28.060
and ensure that contract commitments are supported by realistic staffing, technology,

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.024
and schedules.

00:00:29.024 --> 00:00:33.845
Contract and program teams identify clauses, information requirements, flow-down obligations,

00:00:33.845 --> 00:00:36.255
delivery expectations, and supplier relationships.

00:00:36.255 --> 00:00:42.040
They help technical teams understand what work and information are actually covered.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:47.343
Engineers and architects shape system boundaries, data flows, approved services, segmentation,

00:00:47.343 --> 00:00:50.235
identity, encryption, logging, backups, and resilience.

00:00:50.235 --> 00:00:56.502
Design choices can reduce scope and make required safeguards easier to operate consistently.

00:00:56.502 --> 00:01:01.323
Administrators and IT teams manage accounts, endpoints, networks, configurations, updates,

00:01:01.323 --> 00:01:03.251
monitoring, support, and change.

00:01:03.251 --> 00:01:09.036
Daily operational discipline determines whether documented controls remain true after an assessment.

00:01:09.036 --> 00:01:13.857
Developers and product teams contribute through secure development, controlled repositories,

00:01:13.857 --> 00:01:17.231
dependency management, testing, access restrictions, change review,

00:01:17.231 --> 00:01:23.016
and proper handling of FCI or CUI in development and support workflows.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:27.354
Employees need to recognize protected information, use approved systems,

00:01:27.354 --> 00:01:30.729
follow access and reporting procedures, complete training,

00:01:30.729 --> 00:01:35.550
and avoid moving contract data into unapproved email, storage, collaboration,

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:36.996
or artificial-intelligence services.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:41.817
Security and compliance teams coordinate policy, risk, evidence, monitoring, incidents,

00:01:41.817 --> 00:01:44.227
internal review, and assessment activity.

00:01:44.227 --> 00:01:51.940
Their role is strongest when integrated with operations rather than functioning as a separate paperwork layer.
